  "id": "COMPOUND:32301 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "Dodonolide is implicated in the interaction with HUVEC through multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role in modulating cellular processes in these endothelial cells. The evidence indicates that Dodonolide targets SCCH-26 and Hepatocyte, which in turn are targets of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide and (R)-b-(Boc-amino)-2,5-difluorobenzenebutanoic acid, respectively. These compounds are all known to interact with HUVEC, indicating a consistent pathway of action. The final scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets in the same cellular context implies that Dodonolide may influence HUVEC through a complex network of signaling pathways, possibly involving cell proliferation, survival, or other physiological functions. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Dodonolide could have a therapeutic effect on HUVEC, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the specific mechanisms and biological relevance.",
